<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:09Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal floods 'unprecedented', requires new 'engineering approaches, risk-sensitive urban planning'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c4175a12ef7cd194f279fb8dde1afeab49cd2662513b7324164cf034f7cdf7c</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:52:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning--f18b77019ec7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning" /><summary type="html">Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Dr. Basanta Raj Adhikari, Director of the Center for Disaster Studies at Tribhuvan University’s Institute of Engineering.  He describes the disaster as an illustration of the limits of conventional prevention in the Himalayas. With flood velocities estimated at 170 to 180 kilometres per hour and hazards ranging from ice and snow avalanches to glacial lake outburst floods, he argues that comprehensive monitoring of Nepal’s exceptionally steep and complex mountain terrain is effectively impossible. Yet Adhikari’s analysis is not fatalistic. Instead, he shifts the emphasis from attempting to predict every extreme event toward risk-informed adaptation. Nepal, he argues, should identify high-risk hotspots through satellite observation, supplement these with ground-based monitoring and early-warning systems, and incorporate that knowledge into risk-sensitive land-use planning.</summary></entry><entry><title>Latest flare-up between US and Iran bring conflict's lull to an end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:650ddd031e4699fa83e615d6e0197443eeb54d43a5a05d697dbc7caaa2d7985a</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:08Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:33:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end--9f77617ac27c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end" /><summary type="html">Iran's foreign minister has accused Israel's Benjamin Netanyahu of tricking the United States into war with the Islamic Republic. Over six months into the conflict, there appears to be no end in sight. This after the US struck sites in Iran, prompting Tehran to respond. An April ceasefire brought an end to intense fighting, but sporadic attacks have continued over the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran's closure of the waterway during the conflict has pressured global oil markets, and in turn Donald Trump at home.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Lionel Messi retires from Argentina national team after 21 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbf1b3d3a97c0201abd0e7a741e34d61292f88d741d0adb28c8a58cccae3450c</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:31:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260831-lionel-messi-retires-from-argentina-national-team-after-21-years" /></entry><entry><title>Lionel Messi retires from Argentina national team after 21 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd7272fd9b6e26827190b27d2224b66f0c41cbf5aa12262dd971ac7cf5f1e6ba</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:30:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260831-lionel-messi-retires-from-argentina-national-team-after-21-years" /><summary type="html">Lionel Messi said on Monday he is retiring from international football after leading Argentina to a second successive World Cup final in July.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Canberra's zoo treats its residents to personnalised musical therapy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:241c5142e08879fc713f84861a1c76770f91f4b88229bb093e3c1d693d4e6df6</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:14Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:30:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy--0d0087f76a83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy" /><summary type="html">A music therapist in Australia has been playing for animals at Canberra's zoo for the last five years. It's a relaxing experience for animals and staff alike and the animals all react differently to the music played.</summary></entry><entry><title>As Icelanders say no to resuming EU talks, what issues weighed in the election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2af4297926a94ddc539c65e956f2027503d0b9f3fd57ad7f56b7b3ed0c851930</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:26:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/as-icelanders-say-no-to-resuming-eu-talks-what-issues-weighed-in-the-election--b151c9c282a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/as-icelanders-say-no-to-resuming-eu-talks-what-issues-weighed-in-the-election" /><summary type="html">Iceland's voters rejected restarting negotiations to join the European Union in a referendum that pitted concerns about geopolitical stability against keeping national control of Iceland’s prized fisheries. Talks with the EU to join the bloc had begun after the 2008 financial crisis but had been ended by a Eurosceptic government. But why did Icelanders say no? FRANCE 24's Armen Georgian tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain blames Israel, Russia for spreading disinformation during Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5155b5e8916863b1161dbe9795a06ec5a1bc1ddaa21aeb812da8c6e12412d436</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:24:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-blames-israel-russia-for-spreading-disinformation-during-ceuta-crisis--536350545613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-blames-israel-russia-for-spreading-disinformation-during-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said there were signs Russia and Israel had spread the disinformation over Spain's migration policy that triggered last month's rush of migrants into Ceuta, but no evidence of Moroccan ​involvement. Both Israel and Russia have denied their involvement. Over 72,000 migrants ‌irregularly crossed from Morocco into the tiny Spanish territory between July 30 and 31 ⁠in an unprecedented surge. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal deadly floods: FRANCE 24 report – on the ground with survivors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3442818308ead25d4f4ddd444f543525f6a801f4ebc8c76842067879777b9b93</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:12:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-_-on-the-ground-with-survivors--b891d1208ba1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-%E2%80%93-on-the-ground-with-survivors" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. While rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur in the Nuwako district – one of the villages hit by the flood on August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Northern Cyprus, families wait for news of passengers from sunk ferry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05df192cde461e155bdeabcadd4b0663094a48a69a9d46a925bebed3413e10c6</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:27Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:04:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-northern-cyprus-families-wait-for-news-of-passengers-from-sunk-ferry--efcd34c2b217.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-northern-cyprus-families-wait-for-news-of-passengers-from-sunk-ferry" /><summary type="html">Seven people have died after a passenger boat capsized in Northern Cyprus. 267 people were on board and 23 are still missing. The boat capsized just a few miles off Kyrenia Port in northern Cyprus - a territory occupied by Turkey but not internationally recognised. The ferry has now completely sunk - and the company that operates it says it is "deeply saddened by the tragic accident". It says a hotline has been set up to provide passengers' relatives with information.</summary></entry><entry><title>With no clear contender, "everyone thinks they have a shot"' at succeeding to Macron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd62b91fba3558c0f27961f70582fc843bf0fcc297043b9135fbc10aefe14719</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:56:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/with-no-clear-contender-everyone-thinks-they-have-a-shot-at-succeeding-to-macron--6613716f5c18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/with-no-clear-contender-everyone-thinks-they-have-a-shot-at-succeeding-to-macron" /><summary type="html">There are eight months left until the next french Presidential election, politicians are ramping up their campaigning, with interviews, meetings and public statements. As it gets closer, more and more candidates are vying for a spot on the starting line. For now, far-right candidate Marine Le Pen is topping the polls - what is unknown is who she will be facing in the second round. FRANCE 24's Marc Perelman tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's politicians look to close gap with far right ahead of key election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b540388ceec35446c0099800feb1a87bdefef655567f2025fcedf44ecb609f5e</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:32Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:55:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-politicians-look-to-close-gap-with-far-right-ahead-of-key-election--4e32e88f7c91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-politicians-look-to-close-gap-with-far-right-ahead-of-key-election" /><summary type="html">With eight months until the next french Presidential election, politicians are ramping up their campaigning, with interviews, meetings and public statements. But who exactly will run has yet to be decided. The centre-left socialists and Place Publique parties will hold a primary in October to elect one candidate, as to not dilute the vote. While centrist and centre-right candidates are also having to decide between rivalry and unity. The dilemma? How to best stave off the rise of the far right and left.</summary></entry><entry><title>France gears up for an election year defined by a fragmented left</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6eba90d93202a5841ed0089f31984efbd9f1e13406ad2fbc372b1e08770ebb4</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:35Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:49:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-gears-up-for-an-election-year-defined-by-a-fragmented-left--3c88d139e4b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-gears-up-for-an-election-year-defined-by-a-fragmented-left" /><summary type="html">It's back-to-school week for France, and its politicians are no exception. With a year set to be dominated by a crucial presidential election, both the left and the right wing are hoping to get candidates that will stand a chance against far-right leader Marine Le Pen, who is currently topping the polls. But for now, the political spectrum remains fragmented. So, who is running so far? FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Backstage at Rock en Seine 2026 with up-and-coming British singer Sekou</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ada4e2ea47972e1d5fa38186dc5c3a282033515c63f12755d4cc0463d4ed5aa</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:25:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260831-backstage-at-rock-en-seine-2026-with-up-and-coming-british-singer-sekou--76df5fa84099.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260831-backstage-at-rock-en-seine-2026-with-up-and-coming-british-singer-sekou" /><summary type="html">In this edition of our Arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim takes us backstage at this year's Rock en Seine music festival. More than 180,000 music lovers descended on the grounds just outside of Paris to see 80 live shows. Headliners this year included the likes of American hip-hop star Tyler, The Creator, Australian rockers Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds as well as Britrock legends The Cure, who closed out the weekend in style.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>France and Sweden look to boost European sovereignty through stronger defence ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd4d9ec2a48ed92141f47aec4442dc4e79a3dbabd9df58a0b3c3a9b3457e3ae6</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:22:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-and-sweden-look-to-boost-european-sovereignty-through-stronger-defence-ties--88a1fe36fd43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-and-sweden-look-to-boost-european-sovereignty-through-stronger-defence-ties" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is visiting Sweden on August 31. The aim of the trip is to strengthen the strategic partnership between the two countries. Boosting defence ties is expected to top the agenda, as the war in Ukraine continues and the threat from Russia persists. The newest member of NATO has also expressed interest in joining France's nuclear deterrence initiative.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Football: French forward Bradley Barcola joins Liverpool from PSG in record-breaking Ligue 1 transfer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5007d0f1a071fefe4601bba89f10308ed977094f37f35519b2faf7c0c1708fae</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:18:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260831-bradley-barcola-joins-liverpool-from-psg-for-record-fee--575c8a3efffb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260831-bradley-barcola-joins-liverpool-from-psg-for-record-fee" /></entry><entry><title>Bradley Barcola joins Liverpool from PSG for record fee</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16bcd47d5bdfcd5e577b8992cc1d9a334e712d8d8aded139c7fcfd16c2e39bb8</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:17:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260831-bradley-barcola-joins-liverpool-from-psg-for-record-fee--575c8a3efffb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260831-bradley-barcola-joins-liverpool-from-psg-for-record-fee" /><summary type="html">Liverpool ⁠have signed ​France forward Bradley Barcola ​from European champions Paris Saint-Germain on a long-term contract, ​the ‌Premier League ⁠club said on Monday, making ‌him the latest marquee addition ⁠to their frontline. The whopping fee is estimated to be around £120 million and makes him the most expensive player to leave the French league.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal grapples with destruction and loss in wake of deadly floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb66e001e3d0302d66d5f67f2ab3766b143700b2fc5723e98fff5335dbd19d95</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:10:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods--17641910cea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Nepal have warned of possible fresh flooding after water levels rose in the Bhotekoshi River. The floods took place after a glacier collapse. They have killed at least 900 people - with more than 4,000 others missing in Nepal and Tibet. Now, a massive rescue effort continues and communities grapple with devastation and loss.</summary></entry><entry><title>Executive diversity and inclusion: How to promote female leadership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afc1821383cb4dfbaccba0ee50753dcee207e2d3a30086ad8db3cd5f49702c67</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:51Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:51:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260831-executive-diversity-and-inclusion-how-to-promote-female-leadership--16167a1cd4f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260831-executive-diversity-and-inclusion-how-to-promote-female-leadership" /><summary type="html">CEO Women Europe is a new initiative launched in June of this year to boost partnerships between Europe, the Middle East and the Asia-Pacific region. Kate Moody meets with Sandrine El Khodry, president of this new platform and also Executive Vice President for Global Sales and Marketing at Alcatel Lucent Enterprise.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz accessibility at the centre of US-Iran war flare-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c535d39ff7069fd6d109b992a9a83989995ed84437153f20ab52334744f91d5c</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:54Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:47:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up--9de5d0383172.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up" /><summary type="html">For the first time in a month, the US has launched strikes against Iran. The attack targeted the shipping island of Larak in the Strait of Hormuz. The US says it was aimed at preventing Tehran from placing sea mines in the strategic shipping lane, just days after Washington announced it had completed clearing explosives from there. Iran then reiterated its attacks, saying it had struck two US military bases in Jordan. FRANCE 24's Rochelle Ferguson-Bouyahi tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal races to find its missing as flood area remains largely inaccessible</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87f3ea5767d486ade3ee03c5d697157f69516b98daff8195a9dff28170a6da42</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:15:56Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:41:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible--450be663b9f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rescuers are racing against the clock to find the over 4,000 people missing after the flash floods that devastated an area in the north of the country on August 26. Rescue operations include one where workers are trying to save hundreds believed to be stuck inside a blocked hydropower project. Meanwhile, authorities have started burying unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>The political year ahead in France and the US with analyst Hind Ziane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c56f07f39e7cfa4131ae880f17df0a1215f5ad91b4f60f1fb4597d2864b0b45d</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:00Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:03:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260831-political-year-ahead-france-us-analyst-hind-ziane-midterms-presidential-election--dbd8a92945b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260831-political-year-ahead-france-us-analyst-hind-ziane-midterms-presidential-election" /><summary type="html">As FRANCE 24 kicks off its new season of programmes, we've been looking ahead to perhaps the two most anticipated events to come in the year ahead. In two months' time the US will vote in midterm elections, and in just over six months' time France will vote in presidential elections. In Perspective, we spoke to geopolitical analyst, entrepreneur and international speaker Hind Ziane. She says the midterms will be a real test for US President Donald Trump, while in France it is the parties with clear presidential candidates in place that are currently dominating the opinion polls.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Police arrest Swiss man after deadly rave shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:322e8a653f7316d9e007e0862c630aac176409409f04e4baed82235759a05413</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:03Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:01:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-police-arrest-swiss-man-over-after-deadly-rave-shooting--3916a36cf6c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-police-arrest-swiss-man-over-after-deadly-rave-shooting" /><summary type="html">Swiss police on Monday said they had arrested a 43-year-old man on suspicion of having carried out a deadly shooting at a rave in the town of Aargau Sunday morning. The attack killed a 22-year-old Italian woman and wounded five other people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>After the floods, Nepal's survivors look to rebuilding their lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea40547043a399b29e0352c9cfd1a0f9d8ee0952f7acf2ed3cf22811641e909e</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:53:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives--e039613e514e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. In the devastated villages, families lost everything in minutes. And while rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur, in the Nuwako district, one of the villages hit by the flood of August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Relentless heat worsens Gaza's ongoing struggle to access water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef4ae3fae4455281efdf9938a59842172fee9e481f86d9f565da4eb6598e7f56</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:16:09Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:49:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water--85e6fae055ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water" /><summary type="html">In Gaza, securing drinking water is a relentless daily struggle. The war with Israel has destroyed critical water and sanitation infrastructure, and as temperatures soar, the extreme heat is escalating an already severe shortage into a deadly humanitarian crisis. Two and a half years of war with Israel have damaged or destroyed nearly 90% of Gaza’s water and sanitation infrastructure according to UNICEF.</summary></entry></feed>
